cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "ppsds: probabilistic prediction for stochastic dynamical systems"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for probabilistic prediction on stochastic dynamical systems. It predicts the
  next state of a system as a distribution rather than a point, and implements DRPP --
  distributionally robust probabilistic prediction -- over conic-moment ambiguity sets: predictors
  that optimize for the worst system an ambiguity set allows and carry worst-case guarantees on
  the expected score, alongside nominal and noise-robust baselines. DRPP is one kind of
  probabilistic predictor among others the library is intended to carry: further families of
  ambiguity sets, and the DRPP that matches each, are intended.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Xuzerken/ppsds"
url: "https://xuzerken.github.io/ppsds/"
version: 0.0.2
keywords:
  - probabilistic prediction
  - stochastic dynamical systems
  - distributionally robust optimization
  - conic moment
authors:
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Tao
  - family-names: He
    given-names: Jianping
# The software is the thing being cited above. The papers the predictors implement are
# **references** rather than a `preferred-citation`, because this package is not the artifact of
# a single paper: it holds a family of predictors, and more than one paper contributes to it.
references:
  # This one is published, so it is fully specified below and its DOI resolves. It is the source
  # of the epsilon-logarithm score and of the predictability upper bound the `predictability`
  # subpackage implements.
